s suggests potential issues with cooperation and communication. Also \"unfriendly\" was not in the original notes; it's from Emily's analysis, not a direct note. We must only use explicit candidate facts from our own notes, the public meeting discussion, and public tool answers. Emily's round 1 statement includes: \"unfriendly, eats unhealthily\" but that was part of her analysis, not a direct fact from notes. However, the instruction says we can use public meeting discussion. Emily's statement is part of the meeting discussion, but she said \"unfriendly\" as part of her analysis, not a direct fact. However, it's still a statement made in the meeting, so we can reference it as an observation from the panel. The question asks for observations on crew cooperation and communication style. We have: \"show-off\", \"not open to new ideas\". Also \"very good leadership qualities\". So we can say: He is seen as a show\u2011off and not open to new ideas, which may hinder crew cooperation and collaborative communication. No direct mention of communication style, but we can note that his leadership is strong but his show\u2011off attitude could affect communication. Provide that.\n\nWe must not infer negative from missing info. So we can say we have observations: regarded as a show\u2011off, not open to new ideas, which may impact crew cooperation and communication. Also his leadership qualities suggest ability to lead, but the show\u2011off may affect collaborative environment.\n\nAnswer accordingly."}
