ooperation issues, making B still preferable. Also we need to bring D into discussion soon. So we can say we remain with B, but note that C's stress handling is strong but crew cooperation is problematic, making B still the best.\n\nThus public message: I acknowledge James's info, compare C to B, note that while C handles stress well, his communication and egocentric attitude raise crew cooperation concerns, which are more serious than B's occasional harsh tone. Therefore I keep B as recommendation.\n\nProceed."}
